            <ArticleTitle>Whole-Mount Immunocytochemistry in Xenopus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>pdb.prot097295</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1101/pdb.prot097295</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To visualize the effects of experimental perturbations on normal cellular behavior, morphology, and intracellular organization, we use a simple whole-mount immunocytochemical method with Xenopus oocytes, explants, or embryos. This method is applicable to a wide range of systems, including human-induced pluripotent stem cell-derived organoids, and can be used with both chromogenic (horseradish peroxidase/diaminobenzidine) and fluorescent imaging.</AbstractText>
